.TH FREE 1
.UC
.SH NAME
free \- display memory usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
[
.B \-h
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Free
prints a compact memory summary from kernel
.IR sysctl (2)
data.
The default output is in kilobytes.
The
.B Mem
line reports the total live user process image, including processes currently
swapped out.  On single user-memory-window ports this is more useful than the
resident process size, which is often just the
.I free
process itself.
The swap line reports the logical swap size visible to the kernel swap
allocator.  On systems with compressed RAM swap, this can be larger than the
raw backing store.
.PP
The
.B \-h
option keeps the same units but uses a shorter display for small consoles.
.SH SEE ALSO
top(1), vmstat(1)
